WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.400
- Why would any human being
want somebody to burn out

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.250
and not be happy?

00:00:04.539 --> 00:00:06.956
(calm music)

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:12.693
As I have more attention, I
feel a greater responsibility,

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.933
and so I become very passionate
about creating more context.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:23.880
I think I'm at my best when I
have time to talk like this,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.360
and I'm not when I'm too excited onstage

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.124
or in a one second clip.

00:00:29.124 --> 00:00:34.124
I'm becoming more thoughtful
because I'm surprised

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:39.280
at the sheer level of quick
judgements that our society

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.550
has become comfortable with.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.240
A lot of people out there
that really pretty much

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.750
live their lives based on
other peoples' opinions.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.380
Like happiness and fulfillment
has to become a much bigger

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:53.150
part of the conversation
than financial upside.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.460
I'm always very hurt when
people think that I'm pushing

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.560
hustle and too much work
and make it for the money.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.310
You know, my behavior doesn't map to that.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.250
I would've been a venture capitalist then.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:07.830
Like I'm talking about
actually liking what you do.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.280
There are plenty of interviews
in 2010 where my point

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.010
of view on Crush It
was make $86,000 a year

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.910
and talk about strawberries.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.780
I've been talking about
happiness the whole time.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:23.500
I have evolved and been
forced because I feel

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.570
like I've been dragged
into being a poster child

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:28.580
of something that I don't
believe in and creating clarity.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:33.580
I'm very fascinated by the
conversation of work ethic,

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:35.940
hustle, overworking.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.720
I'm fascinated by people's
ability to not take

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.853
on accountability.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.020
I never feel like my points
of view and my thoughts

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.710
and my hot takes and my
passions and my story are right.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.780
I've never believed that in my life.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:51.820
I don't know if they're right.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.940
I think I enjoy sharing them
because I enjoy sharing them.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.823
I'm a communicator, but
everybody shares that.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.070
I watch these conversations,
I'm fascinated by them.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:05.010
I respect other people's points of view,

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.620
I just, I don't think,
I just want to make sure

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.220
that they don't think
they're right either.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:13.310
A lot of people that push
against hard work, hustle,

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.960
are people who've already hustled

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.770
and didn't find fulfillment from it,

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.960
but maybe somebody else did.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.930
Don't over judge yourself
in every chapter.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:25.140
If you're like working
15 hours a day for a year

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.430
because you're starting
your videography business,

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:30.710
that's probably okay, it does
take work to start something.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:34.000
If you've achieved some level
of success three years in

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.010
and you don't want to take
it to a $10,000,000 business

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.650
from a $3,000,000 business
because you fall in love

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.488
and you've started a family and you want

00:02:40.488 --> 00:02:43.830
to play wiffle ball outside
with your child, that's amazing.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.230
There is no right, there's
only right for you.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.650
I think one of the biggest things we need

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.650
to get more thoughtful about
conversating with yourself

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.790
and trying to develop self-awareness

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.540
and not look for outside validation.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.120
When people email me and say
Gary Vee, I've been hustling

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.880
15 hours a day, I'm like,
you getting enough rest?

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.880
You good? Like, are you pumped?

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.120
Like with intention?

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.630
My intention is to be happy,
and so I'm not gonna apologize

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.330
for enjoying my work.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.430
- Has anybody called
you a minimalist before?

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.270
- No, but it's funny
that you just said that,

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:16.140
like I understand that
about me in some weird way.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:19.630
When I think about anything
I buy, it's 100% for me.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:23.170
Even all the chachkas,
the thrill of finding them

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.610
at a garage sale or like
the one thing I actually buy

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.620
that I think is silly is like
custom New York Jets jerseys,

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.960
but so for me, and it
feels very real to me.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:37.750
Like I don't have outside
things kind of driving me,

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.500
and that's what leads me
to a lot of happiness.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:42.380
I don't care about social
media, I really don't.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:45.180
I care about humans
communicating with each other.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.620
I'm fascinated by communication,
and I'm fascinated

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.730
that we now have a collective
ability to communicate

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.820
on a scale that we've never seen before,

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.380
and I think right now people are focusing

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.280
on the downside of that.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.690
People need to try to be self aware about

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.500
what makes them happy and
doesn't make them happy.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.370
Right now, social media, I
view social media as a mirror.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.170
I think what people are
putting out is an incredible

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:08.960
indicator of what's inside of them.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.940
So right now there's a
lot of political anxiety,

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:15.020
there's a lot of ideological anxiety,

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.460
and so what we're seeing
is a lot of judgment

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:19.813
or forgetting the upside.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:24.160
There's so much love and
greatness going on everyday.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.930
I think humans find what
they're looking for.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:29.600
You're signing into
Twitter to find a fight,

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.360
you're gonna find it.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.670
I think if you go to Twitter
or Instagram to find happiness

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:37.343
and positivity, it's there at scale.

